    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0324" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6511/1284: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Fish</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-02-20">February 20, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155. Your 31, January 15.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d243-f1"/> Following is Legation
                    Bern’s 618, February 16, to Department: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Swiss Foreign Office February 13 forwards following copy note dated
                            February 5 from Italian Ministry Foreign Affairs to Swiss Legation
                            Rome.</p>
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                            <p>‘Ministry of Foreign Affairs has honor inform Swiss Legation that
                                Italian Government agrees to proposal of Portuguese Government that
                                train which takes American diplomats to Portugal may proceed Lisbon
                                or other locality in Portuguese territory where American diplomats
                                shall await disembarkation of Italian diplomats repatriated from
                                United States. Ministry communicated its agreement with above
                                proposal to Portuguese Government today.’”</p>
                        </quote>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>No response has yet been received from German Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d243-f1" n="23" xml:id="d243-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 145, January 19, 7 p.m., to the Chargé in Switzerland, <ref
                        target="#pg306">p. 306</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
